{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg6UB3BWH98jqUFiAyJhd", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "```\nTable 3 reports the estimates, and identity matters. The coefficient on the identity-disclosed indicator is 0.18 (SE = 0.04) in column 2, and it holds up when product fixed effects are added in column 3, where it is 0.15 (SE = 0.05). Reviewer tenure strengthens the effect: the interaction in column 4 is 0.09 (SE = 0.03). Star rating remains a powerful driver throughout, with a coefficient of 0.42 (SE = 0.02) across all specifications. Explanatory power rises accordingly, as R-squared climbs from 0.31 to 0.47 across the columns. All coefficients are significant at the 1% level except the interaction, which is significant at the 5% level.\n```\n\nI kept every number, SE, and significance level unchanged and in their original order. The changes are in framing: opening with the takeaway, saying the identity coefficient \"holds up\" after adding fixed effects, and linking the tenure interaction and R-squared to what they show. \"Powerful driver\" and \"strengthens\" are mild interpretive words; if you'd rather keep the language strictly descriptive, swap them for \"remains positive\" and \"is positive.\""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1875, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1496, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1875}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "19b6103d-cbfc-505f-8dc1-c40cc8379cf6", "uuid": "6d9dab81-ddfa-44c2-a1b8-c23a7426a326", "timestamp": "2026-10-16T19:29:16.275Z", "request_id": "req_011Cg6UB2xMUrTYgCYr8z66o"}
